# Cleanup changes (Phase 1: bug fix + dead code removal)

## 1. Fixed: duplicate `_to_time` in `src/application/leave.py`
There were two module-level definitions of `_to_time`. Python silently used
the second (later) one everywhere, which only parsed `"HH:MM"` strings and
did NOT handle Excel's native decimal/serial time format (e.g. `0.354166`
for 8:30 AM). That handling existed in the first definition but was dead
code. Removed the duplicate weaker definition — the surviving `_to_time`
(originally at line 530) now handles both string times and Excel serial
times, as originally intended.

Recommend adding a regression test for `_to_time` with a serial-time input
(e.g. `_to_time(0.5) == time(12, 0)`) so this can't silently regress again.

## 2. Removed ~145 lines of dead, commented-out code in `src/application/leave.py`
An old row-by-row draft of `apply_leave_kegiatan` was left commented out
directly below the live implementation. Deleted; the live function is
unchanged.

## 3. Removed leftover commented duplicate lines in `src/application/payroll.py`
Four commented-out lines duplicating the active deduction-extraction logic
in `build_payslip_records` were left in as clutter. Deleted; logic unchanged.

## 4. Deleted `src/hr_nicegui/old __init__`
A stray, non-`.py`-extensioned prototype file (never importable — has a
space in the filename) referencing a module that doesn't exist
(`attendance.local_file_picker`). Confirmed nothing in the codebase
references it. Deleted.

## Net effect
- `leave.py`: 857 → 694 lines, no behavior change except the `_to_time` fix
  (which corrects a latent bug rather than changing intended behavior).
- `payroll.py`: 336 → 330 lines, no behavior change.
- Both files verified to compile (`python -m py_compile`).

## Not done yet (next candidates per our discussion)
- Rewrite `apply_leave_kegiatan` as vectorized Polars (currently drops to
  row-by-row Python + schema-less `pl.DataFrame(rows)` reconstruction).
- Replace the 20-positional-argument `run_attendance_pipeline` call with a
  request dataclass.
- Split `build_daily_attendance` in `attendance/engine.py` into named
  sub-steps.
</file>

